<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Armenian Kingdom of Cilicia</h1><p class="st-meta">1080 CE – 1375 CE · capital Sis</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An Armenian kingdom on the Mediterranean that allied with Crusaders and Mongols and was the last independent Armenian state of the Middle Ages.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 1080, as Byzantine rule in the East collapsed, the Armenian lord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ruben-i-prince-of-armenia">Ruben</a> established himself in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taurus-mountains">Taurus</a> mountains of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilicia">Cilicia</a>. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rubenid-dynasty">Rubenid</a> descendants expanded into the Cilician plain, and in 1198 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leo-i-king-of-armenia">Leo I</a> was crowned king with the blessing of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a> and the pope.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilicia">Cilicia</a> combined Armenian traditions with Frankish feudal institutions, titles and law, and its nobles intermarried with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusader</a> families. The port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayas-cilicia">Ayas</a> carried Venetian and Genoese trade in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spice-trade">spices</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hethum-i">Hethum I</a> submitted to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> and travelled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karakorum">Karakorum</a> in 1254, allying with them against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluks</a>. The kingdom produced fine illuminated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a>, notably those of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toros-roslin">Toros Roslin</a>, while the Catholicos resided at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hromkla">Hromkla</a> and from 1293 at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sis-cilicia">Sis</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Repeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> invasions wore the kingdom down after Mongol power waned. In 1375 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluks</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sis-cilicia">Sis</a> and captured Leo V of the Lusignan line, who died in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> in 1393. The title King of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/armenia">Armenia</a> passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-lusignan">Lusignans</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/armenian-kingdom-of-cilicia.jpg" alt="Armenian Kingdom of Cilicia" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Samhanin · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Rubenid_Dynasty.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1080 CE – 1375 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sis</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Leo I, Hethum I, Leo V</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Armenian Apostolic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Armenian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Cilician Armenia, Lesser Armenia (Cilicia), Armenian Principality of Cilicia, Kingdom of Cilicia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1228&amp;focus=armenian-kingdom-of-cilicia" aria-label="Armenian Kingdom of Cilicia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5570 845 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Armenian Kingdom of Cilicia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5890 1101L5709 970M5890 1101L7559 780M5890 1101L6134 1224M5890